cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  strudel-render-study: a two-layer reproducibility study of Strudel's
  pattern and signal layers
message: >-
  If you use this artefact, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Sergio
    family-names: Pulido-Casado
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0020-683X'
    affiliation: Alodai
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Alodai/strudel-render-study'
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.2
abstract: >-
  A companion artefact to an ICLC 2027 submission. Layer 1 queries three
  deterministic Strudel patterns to haps, serialises the exact BigInt rationals,
  and digests them; it is exactly reproducible and identical across darwin-arm64
  and linux-x64. Layer 2 renders one of the same patterns to audio through
  Strudel's own renderPatternAudio under 8-way concurrency; on the host of record
  it is not reproducible, with 26 of 768 renders across four runs producing
  different audio and 15 distinct outputs observed for one fully deterministic
  pattern. The repository ships the patterns as data, the harness as runnable
  commands, the concurrency protocol in numbers, per-batch results at one row per
  render, one canonical and one divergent WAV so the energy comparison is
  checkable, both arms of the node-pool experiment as patches against the
  installed packages, and a control suite in which every mutation arm is shown
  turning red. The cause of the layer-2 divergence is not identified; three
  candidate mechanisms are recorded with their status.
keywords:
  - live coding
  - Strudel
  - reproducibility
  - artefact evaluation
  - Web Audio
  - determinism
